        "to": "The masking asymmetry motivates our focus on cash at the level of the research SETTING, not the unscripted Q&A channel. Stock acquirers have an equity-currency motive to manage their pre-deal narrative (press-release tone, accruals), so a pre-deal signal observed in stock deals is entangled with that documented management; cash acquirers lack the motive, so the cash setting is free of that confound and a pre-announcement run-up documented there reads cleanly, without the competing management story. This is why we focus on cash. We make no claim that the unscripted Q&A is itself more or less managed across arms -- the cross-channel firewall (P5.6) keeps scripted management out of the Q&A on both -- and the cash-versus-stock difference we report is empirical (C6: cash rising; the stock arm a noisy flat null we do not interpret). Motivation for the cash focus, not detection.",
